# Captured source bodies are evidence, not source code.
#
# corpus-selection/pool-<date>.json records a sha256 of each raw body exactly as the CI capture
# received it, and build-inclusion-log.mjs refuses to classify when a hash does not match. Git's
# end-of-line normalisation silently defeats that: w3techs.com serves CRLF, and with autocrlf on
# the committed blob for q4-w3techs.html hashed 19fd6cbf... against a recorded 7deab823..., so the
# integrity check would have failed for anyone who cloned the repository - while passing on the
# author's disk, which is the worst possible direction for a check to fail in.
#
# -text pins these paths to the bytes that were captured.
corpus-selection/pool-raw-*/** -text

# The corpus itself is the same kind of evidence: PROTOCOL.md scores committed page bytes, and a
# rewritten line ending is a different page.
corpus/**/page.html -text
